# Generated documents — rebuild with the Generate button, or:
#   python3 -c "import sqlite3, cv_typst; print(cv_typst.render(sqlite3.connect('db/cv.db')))"
cv.generated.typ
cv.generated.pdf

# Typst build output
*.pdf

# The working database. Not tracked, and this is the point rather than an
# oversight: it is rebuilt from schema.sql plus a seed on first run, and it is
# the only place the `send` table lives — the record of which cut of the CV went
# to whom. The CV itself is published, as db/seed.sql. The application log is
# not, and keeping the binary out of the repo is what keeps those separable.
db/cv.db

# Database backups left by the migrations in db/
db/*.db.backup-*
db/*.db.pre-*
db/*.db.migrating

# Other people's CVs, collected as structural samples — not ours to republish
reference-cvs/

# Python
__pycache__/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Synthetic sample used to exercise the importer
sample-cv.docx
